\begin{equation}
\Phi_{\text{crypto}}(t)
\le \frac{\pi D}{4 \rho L}
\cdot \frac{\mathcal{E}(t)}{M^2}
\cdot \left| \nabla P(x,t) \right|,
\end{equation}
where $L$ is the capillary conduit length and $\nabla P(x,t)$ is the real-time pressure gradient vector logged by Face B sensors. Consequently, any hydraulic turbulence excursion ($\mathrm{Re} > \mathrm{Re}_{\mathrm{crit}}$) dynamically throttles $\Phi_{\text{crypto}}$ to trigger zeroization protocols safely without inducing packet drop or state truncation.
\end{corollary}

